        std::cout << "Irrep " << i << std::endl;

        auto S_q = symmetrize(Op("Sz",0), irreps[i]);
        auto Av = apply(S_q, gs);
        auto b = Av.block();
        auto nrm = norm(Av);
        Av /= nrm;

        auto res = eigvals_lanczos_inplace(ham, Av);
    }
```
Running this, there are two possible errors. The first one after starting the `eigvals_lanczos_inplace` 

` [1]    1356385 segmentation fault  Debug/main ` 

The second one when symmetrizing the operator : 

`munmap_chunk(): invalid pointer`
`[1]    1356051 IOT instruction  Debug/main`

I tried loading the irrep from the toml file directly in the loop instead of prebuilding a `std::vector`, it seems to eliminate error n°2 but error n°1 stays present. 

It appears that this error only happens at half-filling. Everything runs smoothly for any other number of electrons. 

The .cpp file as well as the .tom structure used to reproduce this can be found in this [gist](https://gist.github.com/LeoGaspard/4ce75616a3ec3a0241299bbad9631007)
